    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation first creates a dense feature field from the low-resolution image, then partitions that field into windows without dropping tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into the feature field called F. That field is dense, matching the spatial need stated by the method. The window operator partitions F into X for the next stage. The equation keeps the carrier explicit instead of replacing it with only compact thought.",
